@node Introduction
@unnumbered Introduction

@command{stca-plugin-ariston-remotethermo} is an out-of-tree plugin for
@command{starter-configurable-adapter} (@acronym{STCA}). It connects to
the Ariston Net / Remotethermo cloud, polls live plant data and metering
statistics, and emits them as numeric values into the adapter store.

A dedicated cloud thread owns the @acronym{HTTP} session (libsoup). The
adapter main thread only schedules polls and emits batches. Session
cookies and in-memory caches are process-local; there is no on-disk
state.

Writes for a small set of plant settings are accepted through the
adapter @acronym{HTTP} @acronym{API} (@code{PUT /data/...}) and forwarded
to the cloud on that same cloud thread.

This manual describes how to build, configure, and operate the plugin.
For the adapter itself, see the
@cite{STARTER Configurable Adapter} manual
(@file{starter-configurable-adapter.info}).

