@node Cloud Thread
@section Cloud Thread

All cloud @acronym{I/O} runs on a GLib main loop in a worker thread named
@code{ariston-cloud}. The adapter main loop:

@itemize
@item
starts and joins that thread;
@item
fires a periodic timer at @code{poll-interval};
@item
invokes poll and write jobs onto the cloud context;
@item
emits successful poll batches via @code{stca_plugin_emit_data_ready}.
@end itemize

Poll jobs are coalesced: if a poll is already queued or in flight, a
further request sets a ``wanted'' flag so one follow-up poll runs after
the current one finishes.

@node Polling and TTLs
@section Polling and TTLs

@table @code
@item poll-interval
How often the main thread schedules a cloud poll (default 60s). Live
refresh freshness tracks this interval (@code{live_ttl} equals
@code{poll-interval}).

@item features-ttl / session-ttl
How long cached plant features and login session metadata are considered
fresh (default 12h each). Expired or missing caches trigger a new
features fetch or login.

@item metering-ttl
How long metering snapshots are reused before another cloud metering
request (default 2h).

@item force
When true, live and metering refreshes ignore @acronym{TTL} freshness
(useful for debugging).
@end table

Duration values accept a bare number of milliseconds, or a number plus
one of the suffixes @code{ms}, @code{s}, @code{m}, @code{h}, @code{d},
@code{y}.

@node Live Versus Metering
@section Live Versus Metering

Each successful poll:

@enumerate
@item
Refreshes @emph{live} plant items from
@code{/R2/PlantHome/GetData/...} when the live group is stale (or
@code{force} is set). On refresh failure, a previously cached live
snapshot is still served if one exists.
@item
Refreshes @emph{metering} best-effort when the metering group is stale.
Metering failure never fails the whole poll if live data is available;
a warning is logged and any cached metering values are kept.
@item
Copies every snapshot key into a @acronym{STCA} batch (string key to
@code{STCAValue}).
@end enumerate

@node Data Flow
@section Data Flow

@example
timer / write follow-up
  → schedule poll (main)
  → cloud thread: session + features + GetData (+ metering)
  → in-memory snapshot
  → idle emit on main thread
  → STCA store
  → GET /data (adapter HTTP)
@end example

A successful adapter write for a writable key:

@example
PUT /data/<key>
  → plugin write_value (main waits)
  → cloud thread: Refresh + Submit
  → schedule poll
@end example

