@node Build Against a Local Tree
@section Build Against a Local Tree

From the plugin source directory, with the adapter already built (paths
relative to this plugin):

@example
$ ./autogen.sh
$ ./configure --with-stca=../../configurable-adapter
$ make
@end example

The shared module is produced as @file{.libs/ariston-remotethermo.so}.

@node Build Against an Installed Adapter
@section Build Against an Installed Adapter

@example
$ ./configure
$ make
$ sudo make install
@end example

The module is installed to
@file{$(libdir)/starter/configurable-adapter/plugins/ariston-remotethermo.so}.
The example configuration is installed under
@file{$(datadir)/starter/configurable-adapter/examples/ariston-remotethermo/}.

@node Building the Manual
@section Building the Manual

Info and related targets live under @file{doc/}:

@example
$ make -C doc info
$ make doc          # PDF, if TeX tooling is available
@end example

@node Running
@chapter Running

Edit credentials in the example configuration, then load the plugin with
the adapter @option{-p} / @option{--plugin-dir} and point @option{-c} at
a configuration that selects
@code{<plugin name="ariston-remotethermo">}:

@example
$ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=../../configurable-adapter/lib/.libs \
    ../../configurable-adapter/src/starter-configurable-adapter \
      -c examples/ariston-remotethermo.stca.xml \
      -p .libs
@end example

By default the adapter prints @code{WARNING} / @code{CRITICAL} /
@code{ERROR} only. For plugin diagnostics:

@example
$ G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=ariston-remotethermo \
    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=../../configurable-adapter/lib/.libs \
    ../../configurable-adapter/src/starter-configurable-adapter \
      -c examples/ariston-remotethermo.stca.xml \
      -p .libs
@end example

Or set @code{G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=all} for every log domain.

