@node Required Options
@section Required Options

@table @code
@item host
Cloud base @acronym{URL} without a trailing slash
(for example @code{https://www.chaffolink.remotethermo.com}).

@item user
Account email / username for cloud login.

@item password
Account password.

@item gw
Gateway / plant identifier used in cloud @acronym{URL} paths.
@end table

@node Optional Options
@section Optional Options

@table @code
@item poll-interval
Poll period (default @code{60s}). Also used as the live-data
@acronym{TTL}.

@item metering-ttl
Metering cache lifetime (default @code{2h}).

@item features-ttl
Plant features cache lifetime (default @code{12h}).

@item session-ttl
Login / session metadata lifetime (default @code{12h}).

@item force
If true (or any value other than @code{0} / @code{false} / @code{no} /
empty), ignore live and metering @acronym{TTL} freshness.

@item verbose
If true, enable more verbose libsoup / @acronym{HTTP} logging.
@end table

@node Exposed Values
@chapter Exposed Values

Keys come from two snapshot groups and are flattened into the adapter
store under their cloud or derived names (no group prefix).

@menu
* Live Keys::
* Metering Keys::
@end menu

@node Live Keys
@section Live Keys

Live keys are the @code{id} fields returned by the plant
@code{GetData} response (zone, @acronym{DHW}, plant items, and so on).
Their set depends on the plant features and filters used by the plugin.

@code{PlantMode} is remapped for @acronym{STCA} numbering: cloud value
@code{5} is exposed as @code{2}; writes reverse that mapping.

@node Metering Keys
@section Metering Keys

For each known consumption kind the plugin may emit aggregates:

@example
Metering_ChTotal_Last2h / _Last48h / _Last7d / _LongTerm
Metering_DhwTotal_...
Metering_ChGas_...
Metering_DhwGas_...
Metering_ChElec_...
Metering_DhwElec_...
Metering_ChK24_...
Metering_DhwK25_...
@end example

Which suffixes appear depends on the periods returned by the cloud
(@code{p=1} → last 2h slot and 48h sum; @code{p=2} → 7 days;
@code{p=4} → long-term). Unknown kind codes are ignored.

@node Writable Keys
@chapter Writable Keys

Only these keys accept writes through the adapter
(@code{access} includes @code{w}):

@table @code
@item ChFlowSetpointTemp
Central-heating flow setpoint (cloud parameter @code{U6_3_0_0}).

@item HybridMode
Hybrid mode (cloud parameter @code{U6_12_1}).

@item PlantMode
Plant operating mode (cloud parameter @code{U3}).
@acronym{STCA} values @code{0}, @code{1}, @code{2} map to cloud
@code{0}, @code{1}, @code{5}.
@end table

Other keys are read-only. A write to an unknown or non-writable key
fails with permission denied. After a successful write the plugin
schedules a poll so the adapter store catches up.

@node Adapter HTTP Behaviour
@chapter Adapter HTTP Behaviour

After emit, values appear on the adapter listen port as usual:

@example
$ curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/data
$ curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/data/ChFlowSetpointTemp
@end example

Writable keys look like:

@example
"ChFlowSetpointTemp": @{ "value": 45.0, "access": "rw" @}
@end example

Read-only keys use @code{"access": "r"}.

@example
$ curl -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8080/data/ChFlowSetpointTemp \
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -d '46'
@end example

This plugin does not open a separate plugin @acronym{HTTP} server;
all client access goes through the adapter @acronym{API}.

@node Examples Directory
@chapter Examples Directory

@file{examples/ariston-remotethermo.stca.xml} configures the adapter on
@code{127.0.0.1:8080} and points the plugin at the Chaffolink /
Remotethermo host. Replace @code{YOUR_EMAIL}, @code{YOUR_PASSWORD}, and
@code{YOUR_GATEWAY_ID} before running.

