@node API Overview and Hosts
@section Overview and Hosts

Two brand front-ends share the same Remotethermo backend family:

@table @url
@item https://www.chaffolink.remotethermo.com
Chaffolink web client. This is the default @code{host} in the example
configuration and the fixed @code{Origin} header sent by the plugin
(@code{AR_DEFAULT_ORIGIN}, with trailing slash).

@item https://www.ariston-net.remotethermo.com
Ariston Net web client. Earlier tools sometimes called @acronym{API}
paths on this host while still sending a Chaffolink @code{Origin}.
The current plugin uses a single configurable @code{host} for all
requests (no trailing slash after normalisation).
@end table

Paths fall into two families:

@itemize
@item
Legacy @acronym{R2} @acronym{MVC}-style @acronym{AJAX}:
@code{/R2/Account/...}, @code{/R2/PlantHome/...},
@code{/R2/PlantMenu/...}, @code{/R2/PlantTimeProg/...}.
@item
Newer @acronym{REST}-ish @code{/api/v2/...} routes (features, metering
reports, bus errors).
@end itemize

Gateway identifiers (@code{gw} / @code{gatewayId}) are opaque hex-like
strings (for example @code{943CC6B5A3D0}). They appear in
@acronym{URL} paths and, after the features call, are injected into the
cached features @acronym{JSON} as @code{gatewayId}.

@node Client Headers and Cookies
@section Client Headers and Cookies

The plugin mimics the official browser @acronym{XHR} client. Default
request headers (see @code{ar_setup_headers}):

@example
Accept: application/json, text/javascript, */*; q=0.01
Accept-Language: it-IT,it;q=0.8,en-US;q=0.5,en;q=0.3
Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate
Connection: keep-alive
Ajax-Request: json
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest
Origin: https://www.chaffolink.remotethermo.com/
Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty
Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Sec-Fetch-User: ?1
@end example

@acronym{JSON} bodies use
@code{Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8}.

Authentication is cookie-based (libsoup cookie jar). There is no
@code{Authorization} header. A jar that only contains the
@code{ar.loggedUser} profile cookie is @emph{not} treated as a usable
session; other auth cookies must be present
(@code{ar_http_has_usable_session}).

Login sends @code{rememberMe: true}. Session cookies without
@code{Expires}/@code{Max-Age} may be promoted to a finite max-age so a
text jar could persist them; this plugin currently keeps the jar
in-memory only.

@node Auth Retry Policy
@section Auth Retry Policy

On @acronym{HTTP} status @code{401}, @code{403}, or @code{405}, the
plugin invalidates the session / features / metering caches and retries
the operation once after a forced login (see
@code{ar_http_needs_relogin} and @code{ar_invalidate_auth_cache}).

@node Login Endpoint
@section Login (@code{POST /R2/Account/Login})

@strong{Used by this plugin.}

@example
POST @{host@}/R2/Account/Login?returnUrl=%2FR2%2FHome
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

@{
  "email": "<user>",
  "password": "<password>",
  "rememberMe": true,
  "language": "Italian"
@}
@end example

Expected response is a @acronym{JSON} object with boolean @code{ok}.
Success requires @code{ok == true}; otherwise login is treated as
rejected. Set-Cookie headers populate the jar for subsequent calls.

@node Plant Features Endpoint
@section Plant Features (@code{GET /api/v2/remote/plants/.../features})

@strong{Used by this plugin.}

@example
GET @{host@}/api/v2/remote/plants/@{gw@}/features?eagerMode=True
@end example

Response: @acronym{JSON} object describing plant capabilities. The
plugin injects @code{gatewayId} = @code{gw} into that object and
caches the serialised form as @code{features_json}. That blob is later
embedded verbatim inside the GetData request body.

Cached under the in-memory @code{features} group with
@code{features-ttl} (default 12h).

@node Live GetData Endpoint
@section Live Data (@code{POST /R2/PlantHome/GetData/...})

@strong{Used by this plugin.}

@example
POST @{host@}/R2/PlantHome/GetData/@{gw@}?umsys=si
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

@{
  "features": <features_json object>,
  "filter": @{
    "notEssentials": true,
    "plant": true,
    "zone": true,
    "dhw": true,
    "useCache": false,
    "zone": 1
  @}
@}
@end example

Note that the filter object contains the key @code{zone} twice in the
string built by the plugin (boolean @code{true} then integer
@code{1}), matching the official web client request shape.

Query flag @code{umsys=si} selects SI units.

Response shape (abbreviated; real payloads include many more items):

@example
@{
  "ok": true,
  "data": @{
    "features": null,
    "timeProg": null,
    "items": [
      @{
        "id": "ChFlowSetpointTemp",
        "zone": 0,
        "kind": 1,
        "min": -3277.0,
        "max": 3276.0,
        "step": 1.0,
        "value": 40.0,
        "decimals": 0,
        "options": null,
        "optTexts": null,
        "readOnly": true,
        "error": false,
        "invalid": false,
        "expiresOn": null,
        "unit": "°C"
      @},
      @{
        "id": "PlantMode",
        "zone": 0,
        "kind": 2,
        "value": 1.0,
        "options": [0, 1, 5],
        "optTexts": ["Estate", "Inverno", "OFF"],
        "readOnly": false
      @}
    ],
    "hasAdvancedSettings": true,
    "hasDhw": true
  @},
  "redirectUrl": null,
  "message": null,
  "messageTitle": null,
  "debugMessage": null,
  "resultCode": null
@}
@end example

The plugin stores only each item's @code{id} and numeric @code{value}
into the live snapshot (after PlantMode remapping). Other metadata
(@code{min}/@code{max}/@code{unit}/@code{readOnly}/@dots{}) is ignored
at present.

Typical live @code{id} values observed on hybrid plants include
@code{ChFlowSetpointTemp}, @code{HeatingCircuitPressure},
@code{PlantMode}, @code{AutomaticThermoregulation},
@code{OutsideTemp}, @code{DhwMode}, @code{DhwTemp},
@code{DhwTimeProgComfortTemp}, @code{DhwTimeProgEconomyTemp},
@code{Holiday}, @code{HybridMode}, and zone / operating-mode items
depending on features.

@node PlantMenu Refresh Endpoint
@section Parameter Refresh (@code{POST /R2/PlantMenu/Refresh})

@strong{Used by this plugin} (before each Submit, to obtain
@code{prevValue}).

@example
POST @{host@}/R2/PlantMenu/Refresh?id=@{gw@}&paramIds=@{U-code@}
@end example

Empty body. The official web client also uses @code{POST} (not
@code{GET}). Optional query parameters seen in browser captures
(@code{caller}, @code{rnd}) are not sent by this plugin.
Multiple @code{paramIds} may be comma-separated in the web
@acronym{UI}; the plugin requests one id at a time.

Response:

@example
@{
  "data": [
    @{ "id": "U6_3_0_0", "value": 40.0 @}
  ]
@}
@end example

The first element's @code{value} is the cloud previous value used in
Submit.

@node PlantMenu Submit Endpoint
@section Parameter Submit (@code{POST /R2/PlantMenu/Submit/...})

@strong{Used by this plugin} for writable keys.

@example
POST @{host@}/R2/PlantMenu/Submit/@{gw@}?userActivity=SaveOtherSettings
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

[
  @{
    "id": "U6_3_0_0",
    "value": "45",
    "prevValue": 40
  @}
]
@end example

Formatting rules as implemented:

@itemize
@item
@code{id} is the cloud parameter code (@code{U@dots{}}), not the
symbolic GetData name.
@item
@code{value} is always a @emph{string} in the @acronym{JSON}.
@item
@code{prevValue} is a bare number (not a string).
@item
If either the new or previous value has a fractional part, both are
formatted with two decimal places; otherwise both are integers.
@end itemize

Success requires a @acronym{JSON} object with @code{ok == true}. After
success the plugin updates the live snapshot for the symbolic name and
invalidates the live fetch timestamp so the next poll refreshes from
the cloud.

@node Metering Sequences Endpoint
@section Metering (@code{GET .../consSequencesApi8})

@strong{Used by this plugin.}

@example
GET @{host@}/api/v2/remote/reports/@{gw@}/consSequencesApi8\
  ?usages=Ch%2CDhw&hasSlp=False&umSys=si
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

@{"useCache": false@}
@end example

Despite being a @code{GET}, the official client (and this plugin) send
a small @acronym{JSON} body. Query flags request central-heating and
@acronym{DHW} usages, no SLP, SI units.

Response: a @acronym{JSON} @emph{array} of series objects:

@example
[
  @{ "k": 7, "p": 1, "v": [ /* numbers */ ] @},
  @{ "k": 7, "p": 2, "v": [ /* @dots{} */ ] @},
  @{ "k": 10, "p": 4, "v": [ /* @dots{} */ ] @}
]
@end example

@table @code
@item k
Consumption kind (see @ref{Metering Kind and Period Codes}).
@item p
Period / bucket scheme.
@item v
Array of samples for that kind and period.
@end table

Aggregation performed by the plugin:

@table @code
@item p = 1
Twenty-four 2-hour slots (~48h). Emits
@code{@{prefix@}_Last2h} = last sample and
@code{@{prefix@}_Last48h} = sum of all samples.
@item p = 2
Seven daily buckets. Emits @code{@{prefix@}_Last7d} = sum.
@item p = 4
Long-term buckets. Emits @code{@{prefix@}_LongTerm} = sum.
@end table

Unknown @code{k} values are ignored. Metering failures are logged; a
prior cache may still be served.

@node Related Endpoints Not Used Here
@section Related Endpoints (Not Used by This Plugin)

Documented from earlier Chaffolink / Ariston client work for
completeness. Behaviour should be re-verified before relying on them.

@subsection Bus Errors

@example
GET @{host@}/api/v2/busErrors?gatewayId=@{gw@}&blockingOnly=False&culture=en-US
@end example

Response: @acronym{JSON} array of fault objects, for example:

@example
@{
  "gw": "F0AD4E0590BD",
  "timestamp": "2022-07-14T10:55:04",
  "fault": 45,
  "mult": 0,
  "code": "501",
  "pri": 1053500,
  "errDex": "No flame detected",
  "res": false,
  "blk": true
@}
@end example

@subsection Heating Time Program

@example
POST @{host@}/R2/PlantTimeProg/SetTimeProg/@{gw@}?umsys=si
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
@end example

Body embeds @code{progId}, a @code{weeklyPlan} with per-day
@code{slices} of @code{@{ "from": <minutes-from-midnight>, "temp": 0|1 @}},
and the cached @code{features} object. Used historically to push
predefined heating schedules; not wired in this plugin.

@node Symbolic Names and Cloud Parameter IDs
@section Symbolic Names and Cloud Parameter IDs

GetData exposes human-readable @code{id} strings. PlantMenu Submit /
Refresh use opaque @code{U@dots{}} codes. Mapping known from this
plugin and prior clients:

@multitable @columnfractions .38 .22 .40
@headitem Symbolic name @tab Cloud id @tab Notes
@item @code{ChFlowSetpointTemp}
@tab @code{U6_3_0_0}
@tab Writable in this plugin. CH flow setpoint (°C).
@item @code{HybridMode}
@tab @code{U6_12_1}
@tab Writable in this plugin. 0 Auto / 1 Boiler / 2 HP only.
@item @code{PlantMode}
@tab @code{U3}
@tab Writable in this plugin. See @ref{Enum Remappings}.
@item @code{AutomaticThermoregulation}
@tab @code{U6_3_3}
@tab Climatic / weather compensation on/off. Not writable here.
@item @code{DhwMode}
@tab @code{U6_9_2}
@tab 0 off / 1 timed / 2 always on. Not writable here.
@item @code{DhwTemp}
@tab @code{U6_9_0}
@tab DHW setpoint. Not writable here.
@item @code{DhwTimeProgEconomyTemp}
@tab @code{U6_9_1_0_1}
@tab Economy slot setpoint. Not writable here.
@item @code{IsQuite} (Quiet)
@tab @code{U6_15_0_1}
@tab Quiet / silent mode. Not writable here.
@item @code{HybridTankChargeMode}
@tab @code{U6_9_3}
@tab Tank charge strategy. Not writable here.
@item @code{OperatingMode} (zone)
@tab @code{U0_0}
@tab Zone control strategy; remapped historically. Not writable here.
@end multitable

Browser captures have also used multi-id Refresh queries such as
@code{paramIds=U6_3_0_0,U6_3_0_2,U6_3_0_4} (related CH curve / offset
parameters); those extra codes are not yet mapped in this plugin.

@node Enum Remappings
@section Enum Remappings

Some cloud enums do not match the numbering used on the STARTER /
@acronym{STCA} side. The plugin remaps @strong{PlantMode} only:

@multitable @columnfractions .35 .30 .35
@headitem Meaning @tab Cloud @code{PlantMode} @tab @acronym{STCA} value
@item Summer (Estate) @tab 0 @tab 0
@item Winter (Inverno) @tab 1 @tab 1
@item Off @tab 5 @tab 2
@end multitable

Web @code{optTexts} for PlantMode are typically
@code{["Estate","Inverno","OFF"]} with @code{options: [0,1,5]}.

Historical (not applied by this plugin) zone @strong{OperatingMode}
mapping used by the older Chaffolink service:

@multitable @columnfractions .40 .30 .30
@headitem Meaning @tab Cloud @code{U0_0} @tab ST-side value
@item Off @tab 0 @tab 0
@item Manual @tab 2 @tab 1
@item Programmed / scheduled @tab 3 @tab 2
@end multitable

@node Metering Kind and Period Codes
@section Metering Kind and Period Codes

@code{k} values recognised by this plugin (aligned with
@code{ConsumptionType} from @code{python-ariston-api}, plus provisional
portal codes):

@multitable @columnfractions .12 .40 .48
@headitem @code{k} @tab Snapshot prefix @tab Meaning (best known)
@item 1 @tab @code{Metering_ChTotal} @tab CH total energy
@item 2 @tab @code{Metering_DhwTotal} @tab DHW total energy
@item 7 @tab @code{Metering_ChGas} @tab CH gas (kWh-equivalent)
@item 10 @tab @code{Metering_DhwGas} @tab DHW gas
@item 20 @tab @code{Metering_ChElec} @tab CH electricity
@item 21 @tab @code{Metering_DhwElec} @tab DHW electricity
@item 24 @tab @code{Metering_ChK24} @tab Provisional; seen on web portal
@item 25 @tab @code{Metering_DhwK25} @tab Provisional; seen on web portal
@end multitable

Period @code{p}:

@table @code
@item 1
2-hour samples (24 points ≈ 48h window).
@item 2
Daily samples (7 points ≈ one week).
@item 4
Longer / long-term buckets.
@end table

Units follow @code{umSys=si} (energy series treated as kWh-scale
aggregates in downstream tooling). Exact cloud semantics for
@code{k=24}/@code{25} remain provisional.

